From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shital Shah <2096835+sytelus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:53:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] render: DRM-free mode (surfaceless EGL, shm output
 buffers)

Let Hyprland composite on a GPU it can only reach through EGL (no DRM render node, no GBM, no
dmabuf), e.g. Mesa's d3d12 driver in WSL2, or a VM/CI with only a surfaceless/software device.

- OpenGL: when the backend has no DRM fd, initialise EGL on EGL_PLATFORM_SURFACELESS_MESA instead of
  the device/GBM platforms.
- Renderbuffer: output buffers that are CPU (shm) buffers get a GL framebuffer texture of their size
  and format; after each frame, readbackToBuffer() copies only the damaged rectangles into the shm
  buffer with glReadPixels (GL_PACK_ROW_LENGTH = stride), collapsing many rectangles to their extents.
- GLRenderer::endRender calls the readback for normal (non-screencopy) renders.
- Monitor: an shm buffer is a valid present buffer for the initial modeset, and shm swapchains
  have two buffers, not three: the backend has at most one frame in flight, and allocation on
  shared-memory filesystems is slow (3x 4K at three buffers each took over 10 s to start in WSL).

Nothing changes when a DRM fd exists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
